From b59b4d4e5ea46b9de135532dec50bdaed65d518f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 09:19:16 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Persist authenticated recent header context with disk block
 transitions

Recover child height and MTP from bounded linked history after reopen and disconnect. Store the newest eleven headers and exact body bytes atomically with the state; reject malformed context as an operational error. The context reader binds body header and length, not full transaction validity. Explicit trusted initialization remains caller-owned. Standalone and full-tree disk suites pass; eleven-header rollover remains additional coverage to complete.
---
